      },
      "justification": "Per ACLS guidelines for asystole/PEA, epinephrine 1mg IV should be given as soon as feasible. This is the primary pharmacologic intervention in cardiac arrest and has not yet been administered."
    },
    {
      "action_id": "give_epinephrine_1mg_iv",
